dropped the body
--
C++20 compound requirement `{ E } -> C' ([expr.prim.req.compound]/1):
the return-type-requirement is checked as C<decltype((E))>.  Pre-increment
of an arithmetic lvalue yields an lvalue ([expr.pre.incr]/1), so
decltype((++a)) is an lvalue reference and SameAs<decltype((++a)), int&>
holds.  The type-constraint's explicit argument `T &' (a compound type
naming the enclosing template parameter) is substituted and type-checked
before the concept-id is evaluated; it was passed unsubstituted and the
static assertion "++int is int&" failed.  See
doc/architectural/cpp-requires-expression-support.md.
